<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">One brand, several levels, one end customer at the end</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">An automotive supplier almost never reaches the vehicle owner directly. In between are independent workshops, trade, franchise chains and – in the original equipment business – the vehicle manufacturers themselves. Each of these levels judges the same brand by its own criteria: the workshop asks about availability, fitting and service, the trade about margin and demand, the vehicle owner about safety and trust.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Then there is the international dimension. What counts as premium quality in one market is already average in a technologically more advanced one. Price structures, labelling requirements and trademark law differ from country to country.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">In this business, communication for everyone reaches no one properly.</p>
</section>

